    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0285f55_e3525616",
        "filename": "finder/finder.go",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 1148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-10T20:47:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What kinds of errors would we prefer cause a failure instead of being ignored?\n\nIt occurs to me that if the finder runs successfully, and then one of the directories that it previously scanned is replaced with a symlink pointing somewhere else, then the next run of the finder will try to Stat some directories somewhere else (potentially triggering whatever the errors are that might happen here).\n\nIs this a situation that we care about? (currently what happens is the failures are ignored, and when another goroutine calls Stat on the symlink, it discovers it\u0027s not a directory and disconnects the entire subtree all at once).\n\n(We could validate the parent directory before checking any child directory if it is something we care about; it seems like more work and less parallelism though. We could also have an extra-lax Stat behavior only for directories that were loaded from the cache; I suspect that increases the risk of differing results across runs though)",
      "parentUuid": "4ae18123_bb24c083",
      "revId": "b6d161bf16031e06fc8d532e35a53c73ad20f84f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7629f62_d23bec04",
        "filename": "finder/finder.go",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 1148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-14T22:05:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be nice if a dangling symlink was an error, but I expect that is infeasible, someone probably has a use case for checking in a dangling symlink somewhere in the tree.\n\nIgnoring errors when statting entries in the cache is probably the right thing to do, and marking the node as dirty.  Errors when statting real files on disk should not be ignored, except for specific use cases we need to allow (unreadable :(, maybe dangling symlinks).",
      "parentUuid": "f0285f55_e3525616",
      "revId": "b6d161bf16031e06fc8d532e35a53c73ad20f84f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
